    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Data Collection Facts Label\"\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n<style>\ntable.nutrition-label {\n  width: 75%;\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n  border: 2px solid black;\n  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n}\n\ntable.nutrition-label th,\ntable.nutrition-label td {\n  border: 1px solid black;\n  padding: 5px 7px;\n}\n\ntable.nutrition-label thead tr:nth-child(2) {\n  display: none;\n}\n</style>\n<table class=\"nutrition-label\">\n <thead>\n<tr><th style=\"border-bottom:hidden;padding-bottom:0; padding-left:3px;padding-right:3px;text-align: center; font-weight: bold; color: white !important;padding-right: 4px; padding-left: 4px; background-color: black !important;font-size: 18px;\" colspan=\"2\"><div style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 5px; \">Data Source Facts Label</div></th></tr>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 1. Source Identity </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Source name </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> NCES </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Domain/topic </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> 2021-22 School Survey on Crime and Safety (SSOCS) Public-Use Data Files and User's Manual </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Source type </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> DAT </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 2. Collection Context </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Collector/producer </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Original purpose </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> To produce nationally representative estimates of school crime, violence, disciplinary problems, school disorder, safety policies, and prevention programs in U.S. public schools </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Collection method </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Survey questionnaire completed by school principals or other knowledgeable school personnel; questionnaires were distributed by mail, with follow-up procedures to encourage responses </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Record-creation event </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> A school representative completed the SSOCS questionnaire, reporting on school crime, safety practices, incidents, and policies during the 2021–22 school year. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 3. Observation and Scope </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Unit of observation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Individual public school </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Population or objects represented </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> U.S. public elementary, middle, high, and combined schools represented by the survey's sampling design </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Time period covered </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> 2021-2022 school year </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Geographic area coverage </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> United States, national coverage </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 4. Variables and Data Structure </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Main variables/fields </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> School characteristics; types and frequency of crimes and violent incidents; disciplinary problems and actions; security staff; safety policies; prevention programs; mental health services; staff training; and school climate and safety practices </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Data types included </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Categorical variables, binary responses, ordinal response categories, and numerical counts or percentages; variable formats depend on the question </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Direct measurements </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> School-reported counts or estimates of incidents, disciplinary actions, and other school conditions, along with reported policies, programs, and practices </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Possible proxy variables </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Reported crime and disciplinary incidents as indicators of school safety; reported policies, security measures, and prevention programs as indicators of a school's safety practices </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 5. Documentation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Documentation found </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> 2021–22 Public-Use Data File User's Manual; public-use data files; survey questionnaire; codebook and record-layout documentation </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Stated collection details </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> A nationally representative, school-level survey of public schools. Respondents report school conditions, crime, disciplinary issues, and safety policies. The user manual documents the data files, variable definitions, coding, and guidance for analysis </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n",
